COMPACT_INDEX = "cone_query: Rooted transitive fanin or fanout regions, shared fanin, and output-cone size filtering or ranking.\ndepth_query: Current-design arrival depth measured from the design's legal timing start boundaries to one or more target endpoints, endpoint-depth filtering, global critical depth/path, deepest outputs, and the union of all critical-path gates.\nedit_apply: User-specified fixed netlist transformations, cleanup, renaming, buffer insertion, constant simplification, merging, and gate-basis conversion.\nequiv_query: Whole-design combinational-boundary equivalence between the current design and an original or previous-edit saved baseline.\nfunc_query: Boolean analysis of explicitly named target signals: equivalence, constants, cofactors, dependence, symmetry, expressions, and PI support.\nfunc_search: SAT-based search for unknown signals, operands, or signal pairs that satisfy a requested Boolean function or property.\nopt_apply: Cost-driven optimization that may modify the current design to minimize logic depth or gate count under scope and gate-basis constraints.\nopt_query: Read-only optimization capability or objective query for critical-path depth and gate-count minimization.\npath_query: Directed path and reachability questions between explicit endpoint sets, including constraints, ranking, depth, mandatory nodes, cuts, and direct PI-to-PO connections.\nreport_query: The cached structured report for the most recent edit or optimization, including what changed and before/after deltas.\nsequential_query: DFF D-input enable, hold, feedback, and functional sequential-pattern classification for one or all flip-flops.\nsession_io: Loading one Verilog design, writing the current design, and closing the backend session.\nstructure_query: Current active named-netlist inventory, object metadata, structural issues, one-level direct connectivity, and pin-level fanout."
